      "keyInsight": "We love to judge someone's brainpower purely by the size of their wallet. When a neighbor rolls up in an expensive sports car, we assume they figured out a secret puzzle that the rest of us missed.\n\nBut nature runs on a much messier engine. A reckless driver speeding down a foggy highway might arrive twenty minutes early today.\n\nDoes that make them a master navigator? No, it just makes them lucky.\n\nIn the short run, a wild gambler and a careful thinker can look identical on paper. The true paradox of success is that foolish risk often pays out faster than quiet wisdom.\n\nThe world constantly crowns lucky fools as geniuses simply because their mistakes haven't caught up with them yet.",
