      "content": "Meet Carlos, an emerging markets bond trader who looked like a financial deity. Year after year, his portfolio generated massive cash bonuses. Everyone assumed Carlos possessed an uncanny instinct for global economics.\n\nIn reality, Carlos held a very specific blind spot. He bought risky debt that paid high yields as long as nothing exploded. He had never seen a rare financial hurricane.\n\nNow meet John, a cautious trader in the adjacent cubicle. John bought insurance against rare disasters. In calm years, John looked sluggish, boring, and barely profitable.\n\nManagement questioned his drive. Carlos drove a sports car; John took the commuter train. But the market environment was not testing intelligence.\n\nIt was merely flipping a weighted coin that had not landed on tails yet.\n\nThen the rare storm struck. In a single summer week, the currency markets collapsed. Carlos did not just lose money; he wiped out his entire career gains and blew up his firm.\n\nJohn, the supposed weakling, survived easily and bought cheap assets from the wreckage. Evolution only looks smart across centuries. Across a few seasons, it regularly promotes the least fit survivor.",
